# Stained glass submerged in a walled flat-world water pool (stone basin so
# the water can't spread; an uncontained fill flooded the world and crashed
# the run). Regression scenario for the coplanar water quads water used to
# emit against translucent neighbours (mesh_vis_logic.hpp liquid_boundary).
# Screenshots must be eyeball-compared; the asserts only pin the world state.
# flags 9 = lighting off + fog off so the underwater view isn't murk.
wait_idle 20 6000
fill 1 1 1 16 8 1 STONE
fill 1 1 16 16 8 16 STONE
fill 1 1 2 1 8 15 STONE
fill 16 1 2 16 8 15 STONE
fill 2 1 2 15 6 15 WATER
setblock 8 3 8 MAGENTA_STAINED_GLASS
setblock 11 6 8 MAGENTA_STAINED_GLASS
wait 10
wait_idle 20 6000
assert_block 8 3 8 MAGENTA_STAINED_GLASS
assert_block 11 6 8 MAGENTA_STAINED_GLASS
assert_block 8 4 8 WATER
assert_block 9 3 8 WATER
flags 9
# Underwater view of the submerged glass, slightly from above.
camera 8.5 4.0 6.0 180 14
wait 30
screenshot submerged
# Above-water view of the glass sitting in the top water layer.
camera 11.5 9.5 5.0 180 50
wait 30
screenshot surface
echo glass_in_water done
